  "limitations": [
    "The study focused on healthy young females, which restricted the generalizability of these results.",
    "Only short-time measurements were used, and theoretically, long-term exposure is needed for a comprehensive understanding.",
    "More studies are needed to investigate different vegetation types, floor heights, and distance to vegetation."
  ],
  "minimum_safe_summary": "This empirical study investigated the impact of viewing green space from a high-rise window on urban dwellers' wellbeing, comparing it to viewing urban space. Findings revealed that viewing green space from the 21st floor significantly increased alpha wave power in frontal and occipital lobes, increased parasympathetic activity, and decreased skin conductance, all indicative of relaxation and positive mood. Participants also reported significantly higher feelings of comfort, relaxation, cheerfulness, beauty, color, and attractiveness, and improved mood states (reduced tension, fatigue, confusion, increased vigor, and lower total mood disturbance). The study's generalizability is limited by its focus on healthy young females and short exposure times, suggesting a need for future research across diverse demographics and longer durations, as well as varied environmental parameters like vegetation type and floor height.",
